During the design process, we primarily completed the following tasks:

First, design the security equipment layout diagram to clarify the installation positions of each device;

Secondly, draw the system architecture diagram;

Thirdly, establish the operational procedures for the security system;

Fourthly, define zoning plans to clarify different functional areas.

Additionally, it is necessary to prepare camera placement tables and access control system tables to facilitate construction and later operation and maintenance.

Installation details include specific installation methods, such as mounting transformers or door lock controllers above access control systems, with card readers and door contact switches installed below. For large-scale projects, technical specification documents must also be provided, typically containing detailed descriptions such as power supply requirements.
